    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Week 4: Introduction to Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Looking Back: Week 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Python Programming Fundamentals\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"During the first week, we learned the programming skills required for AI development.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Topics included:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Variables and data types\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Conditional statements\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Loops\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Functions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Lists, Tuples, Dictionaries, and Sets\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Virtual environments and package management\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#### Goal\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Getting familiar with programming concepts for building artificial intelligence projects\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Looking Back: Week 2\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Building AI Applications\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In Week 2, we took a look at how developers build and manage software projects.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Topics included:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Git and GitHub\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Visual Studio Code\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- JSON data format\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Error handling\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- HTTP requests using the `requests` library\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Calling Large Language Models through APIs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#### Goal\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Getting familiar with AI applications communication with external services and APIs.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Looking Back: Week 3\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Linear Algebra for AI\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Machine Learning works with numbers.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Those numbers are usually organized as vectors and matrices.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Topics included:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Vectors\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Matrices\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Multidimensional arrays\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Random number generation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Matrix operations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#### Goal\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Learn the mathematical language used by Machine Learning algorithms.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# What Have We Learned So Far?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"So far, we have acquired three important skills:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"✅ Programming with Python\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"✅ Building software projects\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"✅ Mathematical foundations for AI\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"These skills are the prerequisites for learning Machine Learning.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# From Programming to Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Traditional programming follows a simple rule:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Input + Program\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"     Output\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Example:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Temperature = 38.5\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if temperature > 37.5:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Fever\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The programmer writes every rule manually.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# But What If We Don't Know the Rules?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Consider these problems:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Is this email spam?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Will this customer buy our product?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- What is the price of this house?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Is this image a cat or a dog?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- What word should come next in a sentence?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Can we manually write rules for all possible situations?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Usually, the answer is **No.**\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Real-World Example: Fraud Detection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's look at how a bank tries to catch fraudulent credit card transactions using both approaches.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Version 1: The Rule-Based Approach (Traditional Programming)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A software engineer sits down with a banking expert and manually writes a set of rules based on common fraud patterns.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```python\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Manually coded rules\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def check_transaction(amount, location, time_of_day, typical_location):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Rule 1: Flag if the transaction amount is unusually high\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if amount > 10000:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return \\\"Flag as Fraud\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Rule 2: Flag if the transaction happens in a different country within an impossible timeframe\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if location != typical_location and time_of_day == \\\"3:00 AM\\\":\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return \\\"Flag as Fraud\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Otherwise, let it pass\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return \\\"Approved\\\"\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"- What if a legitimate user goes on vacation and buys an expensive dinner at 3:00 AM? The rule blocks them.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- What if a clever fraudster steals $500 fifty times in a row from the user's home city? The rules completely miss it.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- As fraudsters change their tactics, humans must constantly write, test, and patch hundreds of new rules manually. It quickly becomes an impossible nightmare.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"Past Transaction Data (Amounts, Locations, Times, Device IDs) \\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"+ \\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Correct Labels (Fraud / Legitimate)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Learning Algorithm (Discovers subtle, multi-layered combinations)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Trained Model (Can flag complex fraud patterns humans wouldn't notice)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"#### Why Version 2 Wins:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The computer automatically realizes that fraud isn't just about a single high amount or a weird time;\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- It might be a subtle combination of Device Type + Rapid Successive Micro-transactions + Specific Category of Merchant.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- If fraudsters shift their behavior, we don't rewrite code. We simply retrain the model with the latest data, and it updates its own internal parameters automatically.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# The Idea Behind Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Instead of writing the rules ourselves...\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We provide:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Many examples\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Input data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Correct answers\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The computer automatically discovers the underlying patterns.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Learning Algorithm\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Predictions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Why Did We Learn Linear Algebra?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Machine Learning algorithms do not understand:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Images, Text, Audio, or Videos.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Everything must eventually become numbers organized into the structures we learned last week:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **A Single Sample** $\\\\rightarrow$ A **Vector** ($x$)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **An Entire Dataset** $\\\\rightarrow$ A **Matrix** ($X$)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Images $\\\\rightarrow$ Matrices of pixel values\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Text $\\\\rightarrow$ Vectors of numbers (Embeddings)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# The Journey Toward Deep Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Our roadmap looks like this:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Python Programming\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Software Development\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Linear Algebra\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Deep Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Large Language Models\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Each step builds upon the previous one.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# This Week's Learning Objectives\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"By the end of this week, you will understand:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- What Machine Learning is\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- How it differs from AI and Deep Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- What data, features, and labels are\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Different types of learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- What a model is\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- How models are trained\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- How we evaluate a model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Why overfitting happens\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and Deep Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Learning Objectives\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"By the end of this section, you should be able to:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Define Artificial Intelligence (AI)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Define Machine Learning (ML)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Define Deep Learning (DL)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Explain the relationship between AI, ML, and DL\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Identify which category a real-world application belongs to\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# What is Artificial Intelligence (AI)?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Artificial Intelligence (AI) is a broad field of computer science that focuses on building systems capable of performing tasks that normally require human intelligence.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"These tasks include:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Reasoning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Problem solving\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Decision making\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Language understanding\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Perception\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"AI is **the largest umbrella** that includes many different approaches for building intelligent systems.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"> **Artificial Intelligence is the science of making machines behave intelligently.**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Examples of AI Applications\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Artificial Intelligence can be found in many areas:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Virtual assistants\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Self-driving cars\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Medical diagnosis systems\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Game-playing agents\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Recommendation systems\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Language translation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Robotics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Not all AI systems learn from data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Some AI systems rely on manually designed rules.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Rule-Based AI\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Before Machine Learning became popular, many intelligent systems were built using **rules**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Example:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"IF temperature > 38°C\\n\",\n",
    "    \"AND cough = Yes\\n\",\n",
    "    \"THEN Possible Flu\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"These systems do not learn from experience.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Instead, experts manually define all decision rules.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This approach is known as a **Rule-Based System** or **Expert System**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# What is Machine Learning (ML)?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Machine Learning is a subset of Artificial Intelligence.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Instead of writing explicit rules, we provide:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Examples\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Expected outputs (sometimes)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The computer automatically discovers patterns in the data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"> **Machine Learning is the science of learning patterns from data.**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Instead of programming every rule, we allow the algorithm to learn them.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Traditional Programming vs Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Traditional Programming\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Rules + Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Program\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Answers\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Humans write the rules.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Data + Answers\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Learning Algorithm\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      Model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The computer learns the rules automatically.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Examples of Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Machine Learning is widely used in:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Spam detection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- House price prediction\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Credit scoring\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Product recommendation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Fraud detection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Customer segmentation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"These systems improve as they receive more data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# What is Deep Learning (DL)?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Deep Learning is a specialized branch of Machine Learning.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Instead of using simple mathematical models, it uses **Artificial Neural Networks** with many layers.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"These networks can automatically learn complex representations from large amounts of data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"> **Deep Learning uses multi-layer neural networks to learn complex patterns from data.**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Deep Learning has become the dominant approach for many AI applications.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Why Deep Learning?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Deep Learning performs exceptionally well on complex data such as:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Images\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Speech\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Video\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Natural Language\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Large-scale datasets\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"It has enabled breakthroughs in:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Face recognition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Speech recognition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Machine translation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Autonomous driving\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Large Language Models (LLMs)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# The Scale and Drivers of Deep Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Deep Learning performs exceptionally well on complex, unstructured data because of two main drivers:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **The Data Explosion:** Traditional ML algorithms plateau in performance, but DL models keep improving as you feed them more data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Hardware (GPUs):** Massive computational power allows us to train billions of parameters.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Relationship Between AI, ML, and DL\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The relationship can be visualized as nested circles:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Artificial Intelligence\\n\",\n",
    "    \"│\\n\",\n",
    "    \"├── Rule-Based Systems\\n\",\n",
    "    \"│\\n\",\n",
    "    \"└── Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      │\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      └── Deep Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Or simply:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Artificial Intelligence\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ⊃ Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ⊃ Deep Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Every Deep Learning system is a Machine Learning system.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Every Machine Learning system is an Artificial Intelligence system.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"However, the opposite is **not always true**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Comparing AI, ML, and DL\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Artificial Intelligence | Machine Learning | Deep Learning |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|--------------------------|------------------|---------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Broad field | Subfield of AI | Subfield of ML |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| May use rules | Learns from data | Learns using deep neural networks |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Can work without learning | Requires learning | Requires large datasets and neural networks |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Oldest concept | Introduced later | Most recent approach |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Real-World Examples\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Example 1: Expert System\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A medical diagnosis system based entirely on manually written rules.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"IF fever\\n\",\n",
    "    \"AND cough\\n\",\n",
    "    \"THEN influenza\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Category:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Artificial Intelligence**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"(Not Machine Learning)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Example 2: Spam Filter\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The system learns from thousands of labeled emails.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"It improves automatically as new examples become available.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Category:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Machine Learning**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Example 3: Face Recognition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The system analyzes millions of images and learns facial representations automatically.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Category:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Deep Learning**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Example 4: ChatGPT\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"ChatGPT is built using very large deep neural networks called **Transformer models**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"It learns language patterns from enormous amounts of text.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Category:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Deep Learning**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"(It is also a Machine Learning and Artificial Intelligence system.)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Practice\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Classify each application into the correct category.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Application | AI | ML | DL |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|--------------|:--:|:--:|:--:|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Chess expert system | ✓ | | |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Spam filter | ✓ | ✓ | |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| House price prediction | ✓ | ✓ | |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Face recognition | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| ChatGPT | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Rule-based medical diagnosis | ✓ | | |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Key Takeaways\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Artificial Intelligence is the broadest field.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Machine Learning is one approach for building AI systems.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Deep Learning is a specialized type of Machine Learning.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Not every AI system uses Machine Learning.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Every Deep Learning model is also a Machine Learning model and an Artificial Intelligence system.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In the next section, we will learn about the most important ingredient of every Machine Learning system:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Data.**\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Data, Samples, Features, and Labels\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Learning Objectives\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"By the end of this section, you should be able to:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Understand the role of data in Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Define Dataset, Sample, Feature, and Label\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Identify features and labels in real-world problems\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Understand the difference between Classification and Regression problems\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Why is Data Important in Machine Learning?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Data is the foundation of every Machine Learning system.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A Machine Learning model learns patterns from data and uses those patterns to make predictions or decisions.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A simple way to think about Machine Learning is:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Learning Process\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Prediction\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Without data, a Machine Learning model has nothing to learn from.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# What is a Dataset?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A **Dataset** is a collection of data examples used for training, evaluating, or testing a Machine Learning model.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A dataset usually contains:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Multiple examples (samples)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Information about each example (features)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Sometimes the expected answer (label)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Example:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A dataset of house prices:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Area (m²) | Bedrooms | Age | Price |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|-----------|----------|-----|-------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 120 | 3 | 10 | 350000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 90 | 2 | 20 | 220000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 150 | 4 | 5 | 500000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This entire table is a **Dataset**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# What is a Sample?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A **Sample** is a single example or observation inside a dataset.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Each row in a dataset represents one sample.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Example:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"From the house price dataset:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Area | Bedrooms | Age | Price |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|------|----------|-----|-------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 120 | 3 | 10 | 350000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This row represents **one sample**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In Machine Learning terminology:\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"Dataset = Collection of Samples\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Sample 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Sample 2\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Sample 3\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"...\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Sample N\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# What is a Feature?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A **Feature** is an input variable that describes a sample.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"Features generally fall into two main types:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Numerical Features:** Continuous or discrete numbers (e.g., Area: 120m², Bedrooms: 3).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Categorical Features:** Labels or categories representing distinct groups (e.g., Location: \\\"City Center\\\", \\\"Suburb\\\").\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Features are the information that the model uses to make predictions.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Features are usually represented as numbers, categories, or other measurable information.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Example: Predicting house prices\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Feature | Description |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---------|-------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Area | Size of the house |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Bedrooms | Number of rooms |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Age | Years since construction |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model uses these features to predict the house price.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# What is a Label?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A **Label** is the output or target value that we want the model to predict.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The label is also called:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Target\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Output\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Ground Truth\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Example: Predicting house prices\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Area | Bedrooms | Age | Price |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|------|----------|-----|-------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 120 | 3 | 10 | 350000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Area, Bedrooms, Age\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Label(s): Price\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The goal of the model is to learn the relationship between features and labels.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Features and Labels: General Structure\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A typical Machine Learning dataset looks like this:\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"        Features              Label\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Input Variables            Expected Output\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"          X                        y\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"[x1, x2, x3]   ----->      y\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### During training, the model learns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Features → Label\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#### During the training step, an optimal map/function between features and label is obtained.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Then, after learning:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"New Features → Predicted Label\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#### During the inference step, the achieved map/function is used to predict label for every given feature.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 1: House Price Prediction\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Problem\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Predict the price of a house based on its characteristics.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Dataset:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Area | Bedrooms | Location | Price |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|------|----------|----------|-------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 120 | 3 | City Center | 350000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 80 | 2 | Suburb | 180000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Area\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Number of bedrooms\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Location\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Label:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- House price\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Question:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Input:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Area = 100 m²\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Bedrooms = 2\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Location = Suburb\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Output:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Predicted Price\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 2: Disease Detection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Problem\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Predict whether a patient has a specific disease.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Dataset:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Age | Blood Pressure | Symptoms | Disease Status |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|-----|----------------|----------|---------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 45 | High | Yes | Positive |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 30 | Normal | No | Negative |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Age\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Blood pressure\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Symptoms\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Label:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Disease status\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model learns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Patient Information → Disease Prediction\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 3: Student Score Prediction\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Problem\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Predict a student's final score.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Dataset:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Study Hours | Attendance | Previous Score | Final Score |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|-------------|------------|----------------|-------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 5 | 90% | 75 | 82 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 2 | 60% | 50 | 45 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Study hours\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Attendance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Previous score\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Label:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Final score\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model learns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Student Information → Expected Score\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 4: Email Classification\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Problem\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Determine whether an email is spam or not.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Dataset:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Email Text | Spam |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|------------|------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| \\\"Win a free prize!\\\" | Yes |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| \\\"Meeting tomorrow\\\" | No |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Words in the email\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Email characteristics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Label:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Spam / Not Spam\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model learns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Email Content → Spam Classification\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Types of Machine Learning Problems\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"After defining features and labels, we can categorize Machine Learning problems based on the type of output we want to predict.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The two most common categories are:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Classification\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Regression\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Classification\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Classification is a problem where the output belongs to a specific category or class.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The label is usually a discrete value.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Problem | Input | Output |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---------|-------|--------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Spam detection | Email | Spam / Not Spam |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Disease detection | Patient data | Positive / Negative |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Image recognition | Image | Cat / Dog |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Output examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Yes / No\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Spam / Not Spam\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Class A / Class B / Class C\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Regression\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Regression is a problem where the output is a continuous numerical value.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Problem | Input | Output |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---------|-------|--------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| House price prediction | House information | Price |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Temperature prediction | Weather data | Temperature |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Score prediction | Student information | Score |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Output examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"350000\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"23.5°C\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"87.5\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Classification vs Regression\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Classification | Regression |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|----------------|------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Predicts categories | Predicts numbers |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Output is discrete | Output is continuous |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Example: Spam or Not Spam | Example: House Price |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Example: Disease Yes/No | Example: Temperature |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Practice Exercise\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"For each problem, identify:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Label\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Problem type (Classification or Regression)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Problem 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Predict whether a customer will buy a product.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Possible features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Age\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Previous purchases\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Website visits\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Label:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Type:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Problem 2\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Predict the price of a used car.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Possible features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Brand\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Year\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Mileage\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Label:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Type:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Key Takeaways\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Data is the foundation of Machine Learning.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- A dataset contains many samples.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- A sample represents one example.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Features are the inputs used by the model.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Labels are the outputs we want to predict.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Classification predicts categories.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Regression predicts numerical values.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In the next section, we will learn about different types of Machine Learning approaches and how models learn from data.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Types of Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Learning Objectives\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"By the end of this section, you should be able to:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Understand the main types of Machine Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Explain the difference between Supervised, Unsupervised, and Reinforcement Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Identify the appropriate learning approach for different real-world problems\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# How Do Machines Learn?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Machine Learning systems learn from experience.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The type of experience and the available information determine the learning approach.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The three main categories of Machine Learning are:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Supervised Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Unsupervised Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Reinforcement Learning\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# 1. Supervised Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Definition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Supervised Learning is a type of Machine Learning where the model learns from **labeled data**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The training dataset contains:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Input features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Correct output (label)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model learns the relationship between inputs and outputs.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The goal is to predict the correct output for new, unseen data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## How Supervised Learning Works\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The learning process looks like this:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"Features + Labels --> Learning Algorithm --> Trained Model --> Prediction for New Data \"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"Example:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Input: (House area = 120 m², Bedrooms = 3) --> Model --> Output: Predicted Price = 350000\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Types of Supervised Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Supervised Learning is usually divided into two main categories:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## 1. Classification\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model predicts a category.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Email → Spam / Not Spam\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Image → Cat / Dog\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Patient → Disease / No Disease\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## 2. Regression\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model predicts a numerical value.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"House → Price\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Weather → Temperature\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Student Information → Final Score\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Real-World Applications of Supervised Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Spam Detection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Input:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Email text\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Sender information\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Email features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Output:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Spam\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Not Spam\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Medical Diagnosis\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Input:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Patient information\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Medical measurements\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Output:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Disease category\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Price Prediction\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Input:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- House features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Market information\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Output:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Estimated price\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# 2. Unsupervised Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Definition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Unsupervised Learning is a type of Machine Learning where the model learns from **unlabeled data**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The dataset contains only input features.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"There are no predefined answers.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The goal is to discover hidden patterns, structures, or relationships in the data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## How Unsupervised Learning Works\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Data (No Labels) --> Learning Algorithm --> Discover Patterns\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model tries to answer questions such as:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Are there groups in this data?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Which examples are similar?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Are there unusual patterns?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example: Customer Segmentation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A company has information about customers:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Age | Income | Purchase History |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|-----|--------|------------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 25 | Low | Few purchases |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 45 | High | Many purchases |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 30 | Medium | Regular purchases |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"There are no predefined customer groups.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The algorithm may discover groups such as:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Group 1:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Young customers with low spending\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Group 2:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"High-income frequent buyers\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Group 3:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Occasional customers\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Common Tasks in Unsupervised Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Clustering\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Grouping similar data points together.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Customer segmentation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Grouping news articles\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Organizing documents\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Dimensionality Reduction\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Reducing the number of features while preserving important information.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Data visualization\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Feature compression\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Real-World Applications of Unsupervised Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Customer Segmentation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Companies group customers based on behavior.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Used for:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Marketing strategies\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Personalized recommendations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Recommendation Systems\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Finding similar users or products.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Movie recommendations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Product suggestions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Anomaly Detection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Finding unusual patterns.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Detecting unusual financial transactions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Finding network problems\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Semi-Supervised Learning (The Hybrid Approach)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"What if labeling data is too expensive, but you have millions of unlabeled examples?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Semi-Supervised Learning** combines a small amount of labeled data with a large amount of unlabeled data during training.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Photo Tagging (e.g., Apple/Google Photos):** The system automatically clusters similar-looking faces together (**Unsupervised**), and then asks you to provide a name label just once (**Supervised**) to tag that person across all photos.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Email Spam Detection:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    -  Only a small number of emails are manually labeled as \\\"spam\\\" or \\\"not spam.\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    -  Millions of unlabeled emails help the model learn common patterns and improve spam detection.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Medical Image Analysis:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    - Doctors label only a limited number of X-rays, MRIs, or CT scans because labeling is expensive.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    - The model uses thousands of unlabeled medical images to improve disease detection.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Speech Recognition:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    - A small set of audio recordings has accurate transcripts.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    - A much larger collection of unlabeled speech recordings helps the model recognize accents pronunciations, and speech patterns.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- \"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# 3. Reinforcement Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Definition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Reinforcement Learning is a type of Machine Learning where an **agent learns by interacting with an environment**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The agent makes decisions and receives feedback in the form of:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Rewards\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Penalties\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The goal is to learn actions that maximize long-term rewards.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Reinforcement Learning Components\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A reinforcement learning system contains:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Agent\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The learner or decision maker.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Example:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Robot\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Game player\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Autonomous vehicle\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Environment\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The world where the agent operates.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- A game\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- A road\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- A simulated environment\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Action\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A decision made by the agent.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Move left\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Accelerate\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Select an option\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Reward\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Feedback received after an action.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Positive reward: Good decision\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Negative reward: Bad decision\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Reinforcement Learning Process\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"    Environment\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"         ↑\\n\",\n",
    "    \"         \\n\",\n",
    "    \"      Action\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"         ↑\\n\",\n",
    "    \"         \\n\",\n",
    "    \"      Agent\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"         ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      Reward\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The agent learns through repeated interactions.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Examples of Reinforcement Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Game Playing\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"An AI agent learns to play a game.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Examples:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Winning moves receive rewards.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Losing moves receive penalties.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The system improves through experience.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Robotics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A robot learns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- How to move\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- How to avoid obstacles\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- How to complete tasks\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Autonomous Driving\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A vehicle learns decision-making strategies:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Speed control\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Lane selection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Navigation decisions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Comparing Learning Types\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Feature | Supervised Learning | Unsupervised Learning | Reinforcement Learning |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---------|---------------------|-----------------------|------------------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Data Type | Labeled data | Unlabeled data | Interaction data |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Learning Method | Learn from examples | Find hidden patterns | Learn from rewards |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Human Feedback | Direct labels | No labels | Reward signals |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Main Goal | Predict outputs | Discover structures | Maximize rewards |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Output | Prediction | Groups or patterns | Best actions |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Example | Spam detection | Customer segmentation | Game playing |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Choosing the Right Learning Approach\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Problem: Predict house price\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Available:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- House features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Historical prices\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Solution:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Supervised Learning**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Because we have labeled examples.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Problem: Group customers by behavior\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Available:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Customer activity data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- No predefined groups\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Solution:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Unsupervised Learning**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Because we want to discover patterns.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Problem: Train a robot to walk\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Available:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Environment\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Rewards for successful actions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Solution:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Reinforcement Learning**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Because the agent learns through interaction.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Key Takeaways\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Supervised Learning learns from labeled examples.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Unsupervised Learning discovers hidden patterns from unlabeled data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Reinforcement Learning learns through interaction and rewards.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The type of data and the goal of the problem determine the appropriate learning approach.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In the next section, we will learn what a **Machine Learning model** is and how a model learns from data.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Model Evaluation, Underfitting, and Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Learning Objectives\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"By the end of this section, you should be able to:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Understand why a Machine Learning model must be evaluated\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Distinguish between training and testing performance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Define underfitting and overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Explain why both are undesirable\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Understand the concept of model generalization\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Why Do We Evaluate a Model?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Training a Machine Learning model is only the first step.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The real question is:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"> **How do we know if the model has learned correctly?**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A model should not only perform well on the data it has already seen, but also make accurate predictions on **new, unseen data**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This ability is called **generalization**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Generalization\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A good Machine Learning model learns the **underlying patterns** in the data rather than simply memorizing the training examples.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Training Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Learning\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Good Model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"New Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Accurate Predictions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The primary goal of Machine Learning is **good generalization**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Training Performance vs Testing Performance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"When evaluating a model, we usually compare its performance on two datasets.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Training Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The data used to teach the model.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model has already seen these examples during learning.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Test Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"New data that was **never shown** during training.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model must make predictions using only what it has learned.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A good model should perform well on **both** datasets.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Measuring Model Performance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"To evaluate a model, we compare:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The model's prediction\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The correct answer (Ground Truth)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Example:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Actual | Prediction |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---------|------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Spam | Spam |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Not Spam | Spam |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Spam | Spam |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Not Spam | Not Spam |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Some predictions are correct.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Some are incorrect.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The more correct predictions, the better the model.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Accuracy\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"One of the simplest evaluation metrics is **Accuracy**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Accuracy measures the percentage of correct predictions.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Example:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"100 predictions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"92 correct\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"8 incorrect\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Accuracy = 92%\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Higher accuracy generally indicates better performance.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"However, accuracy alone is **not always sufficient**, especially for imbalanced datasets.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In future lessons, we will learn additional evaluation metrics such as Precision, Recall, and F1 Score.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Prediction Error\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Instead of measuring correct predictions, we can also measure **prediction error**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The objective during training is to minimize this error.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Smaller Error\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Better Predictions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Machine Learning algorithms continuously adjust their parameters to reduce prediction error.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# A Good Model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A good model should:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Learn useful patterns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Ignore random noise\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Perform well on unseen data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The challenge is finding the right balance.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Underfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Definition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Underfitting** occurs when a model is **too simple** to learn the underlying patterns in the data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"It fails to capture important relationships.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"As a result:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Poor performance on training data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Poor performance on test data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Characteristics of Underfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Model is too simple\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- High prediction error\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Poor accuracy\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Cannot capture the complexity of the problem\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Simple Model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Learns Too Little\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Poor Predictions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example of Underfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Suppose house prices depend on:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Area\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Location\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Number of bedrooms\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Age\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Neighborhood quality\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"But the model uses only:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"House Price = Area\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model ignores important information.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Its predictions will often be inaccurate.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Causes of Underfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Possible reasons include:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Model is too simple\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Too few features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Insufficient training\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Poor feature engineering\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# How to Reduce Underfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Possible solutions:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Use a more powerful model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Train longer\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Add informative features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Improve data representation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Definition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Overfitting** occurs when a model learns the training data **too well**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Instead of learning general patterns, it memorizes the training examples, including random noise.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"As a result:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Excellent performance on training data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Poor performance on unseen data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Characteristics of Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Model is too complex\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Very low training error\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- High testing error\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Poor generalization\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Complex Model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"       ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Memorizes Training Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"       ↓\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Fails on New Data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example of Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Imagine a teacher gives students exactly one set of practice questions.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Student A memorizes every answer without understanding the concepts.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"During the practice exam, the student gets every question correct.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"However, in the real exam with different questions, the student performs poorly.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The student memorized instead of learning.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"An overfitted model behaves in the same way.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Causes of Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Common causes include:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Model is too complex\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Too many parameters\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Too little training data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Learning noise instead of patterns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# How to Reduce Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Common techniques include:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Collect more training data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Simplify the model\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Remove unnecessary features\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Stop training earlier (Early Stopping)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Apply Regularization\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Use Data Augmentation (for images)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Validate the model during training\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"These techniques will be discussed later in the course.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Underfitting vs Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Underfitting | Good Fit | Overfitting |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---------------|----------|-------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Too simple | Balanced complexity | Too complex |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Learns too little | Learns useful patterns | Memorizes training data |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| High training error | Low training error | Very low training error |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| High testing error | Low testing error | High testing error |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Poor generalization | Good generalization | Poor generalization |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Visual Interpretation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                 Model Complexity\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                        →\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Underfitting ---- Good Fit ---- Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"As model complexity increases:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Performance first improves.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Eventually it becomes too complex.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Generalization begins to decrease.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Generalization is the Goal\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The objective of Machine Learning is **not** to memorize the training dataset.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The objective is to build models that perform well on **new, unseen data**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A successful model:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Learns meaningful patterns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Ignores random noise\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Makes reliable predictions on future data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Summary\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Concept | Description |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|----------|-------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Evaluation | Measuring how well a model performs |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Training Data | Data used for learning |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Test Data | Unseen data used for evaluation |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Accuracy | Percentage of correct predictions |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Error | Difference between prediction and ground truth |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Underfitting | Model is too simple to learn the data |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Overfitting | Model memorizes the training data |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Generalization | Ability to perform well on unseen data |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Key Takeaways\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Training performance alone is **not enough**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- A model should perform well on unseen data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Underfitting happens when the model learns too little.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Overfitting happens when the model memorizes the training data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The goal is to achieve **good generalization**, where the model captures the true patterns in the data without memorizing noise.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 1: House Price Prediction\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Suppose we want to predict house prices using the following features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Area\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Number of bedrooms\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Age of the house\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"We train three different models.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Model A\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Predictions:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Actual Price | Predicted Price |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|--------------|----------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 250,000 | 260,000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 320,000 | 300,000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 410,000 | 395,000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model makes reasonable predictions for both training and new houses.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"✅ This is a **Good Fit**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Model B\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Predictions:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Training Data | Error |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|--------------|-------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| House 1 | High |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| House 2 | High |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| House 3 | High |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model cannot even fit the training data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Its predictions are poor for every house.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"❌ This is **Underfitting**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Reason:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The model is too simple.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Model C\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Training Results:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| House | Actual | Predicted |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|--------|--------|-----------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 1 | 250,000 | 250,000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 2 | 320,000 | 320,000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 3 | 410,000 | 410,000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Perfect!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Now test it on new houses:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Actual | Predicted |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|---------|-----------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 350,000 | 450,000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| 280,000 | 180,000 |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Very poor performance.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"❌ This is **Overfitting**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model memorized the training houses instead of learning general pricing patterns.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 2: Student Exam Prediction\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Suppose we want to predict whether a student will pass an exam.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Features:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Study hours\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Attendance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Previous grades\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Label:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Pass\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Fail\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Underfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model predicts:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Every student will PASS.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Obviously, this is too simple.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Many predictions will be incorrect.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model memorizes every student from last year's class.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"It predicts perfectly for those students.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"However, when new students arrive next semester, its predictions become inaccurate.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model learned the students instead of learning the relationship between study habits and exam success.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 3: Spam Detection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Suppose we build a spam classifier.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Training emails:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Win a FREE iPhone!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Claim your prize!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Limited-time offer!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Underfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model simply labels every email as:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Not Spam\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Many spam emails are missed.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model memorizes exact training emails.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"When it receives:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Congratulations!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"You have won a free laptop!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"it predicts:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Not Spam\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"because this exact sentence was never seen before.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model memorized instead of learning general spam patterns.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example 4: Face Recognition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Suppose we train a model using only ten pictures of one person.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Underfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model cannot even recognize those ten pictures correctly.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"It has learned too little.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The model recognizes only the exact training photos.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"If the person changes:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- hairstyle\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- glasses\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- lighting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- camera angle\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"the model fails.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"It memorized the training images instead of learning facial features.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Analogy: Studying for an Exam\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Imagine three students preparing for the final exam.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Student A — Underfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Reads only one page.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Doesn't understand the concepts.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Performs poorly on the exam.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This is **Underfitting**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Student B — Good Fit\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Understands the concepts.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Solves many different exercises.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Can answer new questions.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This is **Good Generalization**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Student C — Overfitting\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Memorizes every homework solution.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Gets perfect scores on homework.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Cannot solve new exam questions.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This is **Overfitting**.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Comparing the Three Cases\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Situation | Training Performance | Test Performance | Conclusion |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|-----------|----------------------|------------------|------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Underfitting | Poor | Poor | Model is too simple |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Good Fit | Good | Good | Desired model |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Overfitting | Excellent | Poor | Model memorizes data |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Discussion\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Consider the following applications.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"For each one, discuss what underfitting and overfitting might look like.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- House price prediction\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Email spam detection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Disease diagnosis\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Face recognition\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Movie recommendation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Questions**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. What would an underfitted model do?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. What would an overfitted model do?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Which model would you deploy in a real application?\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
